    "name": "Ch 21 - Mock Examples",
    "description": "Chapter 21, section *Mock servers*. Each request has a saved example. Create a Postman mock server from this collection, put the mock URL in an environment as baseUrl, and the requests get the saved examples back. Against the practice API, the two user requests pass their tests and the planned loyalty endpoint answers 404 (it is not built yet).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Get user 1",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 and the body is user 1', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(1);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().name).to.eql('Asha Rao');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/1",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "users",
            "1"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Has a saved example \"User found\" (a real response)."
      },
